        "mission_intent": "We need to develop a comprehensive final incident report template aligned with the NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 2 incident handling lifecycle for use across all SOC teams. The template must cover the full incident response process from initial detection through post-incident activity, including an executive summary section that articulates what occurred, how formal incident response capabilities helped or would have helped mitigate risk and limit damage more quickly. It should incorporate sections for documenting affected data, applications, and services, confirmation that all impacted systems have been returned to normal operations, and a structured timeline of response actions taken. The template needs to support the updated attack vector categories from the current revision, integrate the expanded incident metrics list for measuring response effectiveness, and include fields for identifying attacking hosts rather than focusing on attacker attribution. Additionally, the report format should facilitate information sharing with external parties such as US-CERT and ISACs consistent with our coordination obligations, and the executive summary should be suitable for leadership briefing without requiring technical background. Please have a draft ready for review by the incident response team leads by end of next week so we can pilot it during our upcoming tabletop exercise.",
